theta[6]  6.049 6.757  -8.682 2.099  6.399 10.380 18.673  73640.433 1.000
theta[7] 10.686 6.844  -1.223 6.089 10.066 14.647 26.066  18844.360 1.000
theta[8]  8.416 7.954  -7.193 3.768  8.143 12.738 25.671  87646.977 1.000
mu        7.883 5.207  -2.169 4.589  7.845 11.139 18.279  39607.885 1.000
tau       6.722 5.627   0.462 2.633  5.379  9.245 20.846   7571.285 1.001

And here's what we have now for ESS for tau:

n.iter  ESS
1000  55
10000  450
100000  990

1000000  7500

The inferences all look basically reasonable

Does the sublinear growth of ESS as a function of n.iter suggest that the Nuts tuning is actually getting _worse_ when we have more time in the warmup phase?  Giving Nuts enough rope to hang itself??

A

