That's an interesting possibility.  In the command-line
version, that information gets printed out to the CSV
file.  Depth of tree (log2 # of steps) gets dumped as does
the value of epsilon at each iteration (to account for
when it varies).  Also, the tuning parameters get dumped
as comments.

You can also track it down by setting the number of
warmup steps to 50

The way I get that info should be clear from the command
information -- I pushed most of it into an abstract base
class for HMC and then implemented versions in each of the
cases to write out alternative parameters.  Rather than
writing to an output stream, they could just be returned as
numbers, too.

- Bob

