> Does anyone know how to make the calls to run Stan parallel
> under R?
>
> mcmc::chains is thread safe for writing samples from different
> chains -- I don't know about Jiqiang's extensions.

For now, run multiple chains inside a call of stan only need to compile the c++ code once.
But each of the following call of stan need to compile the c++ code

stan(model.code = , data = , ...)
stan(model.code = , data = , ...)

I think we need some cache mechanism to make it possible to compile the code once if model.code (or file) is the same for another call.  This is doable, it is a bit like http://ccache.samba.org/ then.

Another simpler appoach not to compile c++ code a second time for calling stan for the same model is to feed the result of the first time to later call such as the following (it is just a thought, that is, not implemented).  How does this look?

fit <- stan(model.code = , data = ,....)
fit2 <- stan(fit, .....)

As I am not using mcmc::chains, actually I could use any parallel approaches based on multiple processes R has such as multicore (http://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/multicore/index.html), but even multicore may not work on all platforms.  I am not sure how easy it is to make it just an option.

