The approach below (where I assume the object code (or a link to the location of the object code?) is saved in the fit object) would be fine, in some ways that is preferable in that it is a reminder that we're refitting the model, thus for example we fit the model once, then try again, etc.

I think it would be also good, if it were possible, for the regular stan() call to search for the object code and use it if possible.  But maybe that is not so necessary if your code below works.  I'd have to see how it goes when running.

I do think that some version of not-requiring-recompiling is important, expecially for little models where the compile time is longer than runtime.

A

