I should've thought more about the overall setup.
I'm pretty sure Jiqiang integrated Stan using dynamic
linking so that it's running Stan in the same process
as R.  That would require us sorting out multi-platform
threading on the C++ side and using thread-safe versions
of auto-dif.

If we are just executing Stan in a new process, then
we just want to be able to call four processes in parallel
and wait until they all finish (or two by two, etc. -- max
concurrency and total number of chains are independent).

- Bob

