cpp produces markers in the output which indicate the file and line where things came from.  It would take a little work to keep track of them, but they could be parsed.

> I'm very anti-macro, though, as it makes things
> very hard to debug, even if we get line numbers right.
>
> I'd rather introduce simple macro-like function
> definitions.  If we have syntax that's context dependent,
> the issue is whether we could reuse it or not.

It's true macros are kind of a brute force solution.  That said, I'm not sure you can get much more without a huge amount of complexity precisely because of the context dependence.  Since expressions can have different interpretations, you'd need to effectively replace them locally and parse the replaced expression which gets you back to macros.

Cheers,
Marcus

