Daniel's tracked the source of the throw down to
Boost's lgamma function, which doesn't like values
very close to -1.

I'm guessing the vari memory issue is because the
crash happens at a point where we're trying to
allocate a new vari.

The dump() implementation probably deserves some
further investigation.  It keeps references to the
data to avoid some copying (but then I think it copies
anyway given our use of Eigen Map).

- Bob

