On Thursday, August 30, 2012 10:18:24 PM UTC-4, Andrew Gelman wrote:
> To me it's important becausee it's n_chains, n_iter, n_warmup, n_thin.

At the moment, the command-line arguments to Stan include iter, warmup, and thin but there is no chains argument. Breaking the code for anyone who has used a prerelease of Stan is not a huge cost, but I don't really see much benefit of prefixing n_ to them. Although if we think n_warmup is better than warmup, then I would agree we should prefix all of them with n_ .

Ben

